Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["TensorNetworkFindContractionPath", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976071502187851*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e35a300f-7f8c-4057-9aa6-\
cb3ad44470b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finds an optimized contraction path using the Cotengra library.\n- ",
 StyleBox["Optimal",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": The optimizer method that tries to find the best possible contraction \
order for the chosen objective (often slower/more exhaustive than \
heuristics).\n- ",
 StyleBox["flops",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Minimize total arithmetic work over the whole contraction (sum of \
operation counts across all contraction steps). Good if compute is the \
bottleneck.\n- ",
 StyleBox["size",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Minimize the peak size of any single intermediate tensor created during \
the contraction (a proxy for peak memory needed). Good if you\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]re memory-limited.\n- ",
 StyleBox["max",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Minimize the cost of the single most expensive contraction step (the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]worst\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] step). Good if you want \
to avoid one step dominating runtime or failing due to a huge intermediate.\n\
- ",
 StyleBox["write",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Minimize total memory written/moved for intermediates (roughly the sum of \
sizes of all intermediate tensors produced). Good if memory bandwidth or \
storing intermediates (e.g., for backprop) is costly.\n- ",
 StyleBox["combo",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Minimize a weighted combination of compute and memory traffic, typically: \
total_flops + \[Alpha]  total_write. This trades off computation vs bandwidth \
with a tunable weight \[Alpha].\n- ",
 StyleBox["limit",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Minimize a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]per-step bottleneck\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] score that penalizes steps that are either too \
compute-heavy or too memory-traffic-heavy, typically aggregating something \
like max(step_flops, \[Alpha] * step_write) over steps. This aims to avoid \
any contraction step being an extreme outlier in either compute or memory \
cost.\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976075763503169*^9, 3.976075806234371*^9}, 
   3.9761184401044683`*^9, {3.976138401409347*^9, 3.9761384486475267`*^9}, 
   3.976138481989006*^9},ExpressionUUID->"0d6ab6d9-c98f-4653-8a47-\
b0e58680dfa2"],

